    "provenance": "RAL publishes no free sRGB value for any Classic colour (it sells a digital library, RGB and Lab, from its shop), so these are Wikipedia's approximations, and the page itself says on-screen samples are not binding. Every RAL Classic code the page lists: 215 from the Hex triplet column of its overview table, 'All colours defined in RAL Classic', and two the overview leaves out, RAL 6031 and RAL 6039, from the Sample column of its Green colour-group table. Each code names its source and the date it was read. The forty codes chosen in round 33 were read on 2026-09-13 from the same revision and are unchanged; the page's colour-group tables give other values for RAL 9003 and RAL 9005, and its overview gives two for RAL 9022, and the overview's Hex triplet column is taken throughout. Pearl, metallic and luminous colours are marked `effect`, from their names on the page: fifteen Pearl, the two aluminium colours (RAL 9006, RAL 9007), six Luminous. decisions.md D15, round 92."
